course: dictionary
lesson: 14436
title: Pageant: a show, a contest or a display
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word pageant is a good example. «Our class put on a nativity pageant about the first Christmas.» Here the words nativity and Christmas tell you a pageant is a show where people dress up and act out a story.
explain: Now read this: «The beauty pageant was judged on Saturday.» The word beauty tells you a pageant can also be a contest, where people are judged. The clue is in the words around it. Always ask: what meaning fits this sentence best?
explain: A pageant can also be a grand, colourful display, like «The parade was a pageant of colour.» Here nothing is acted out and nobody is judged. The word colour tells you it means something beautiful to look at. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A pageant is a show or procession where people dress up and act out scenes from history or stories.
fact: A pageant can also be a beauty contest, especially in the USA.
fact: A pageant can mean a grand, colourful display.
fact: «Pageant» is a noun: one pageant, two pageants.
exercise: «The town held a pageant to show scenes from its history.» What is a pageant in this sentence? | A long walk up a hill | A test of spelling | *A show where people dress up and act out scenes from history
exercise: «The parade was a pageant of colour.» What does pageant mean here? | A lost bag | *A grand, colourful display | A cold, grey day
exercise: Mia says, «In the USA, a pageant is a beauty contest.» Which meaning is she giving? | A small pet | A kind of train | A school trip | *A beauty contest
test: «Our class performed a nativity pageant about the first Christmas.» What is a nativity pageant? | A long holiday by the sea | A maths quiz about numbers | A thick winter coat | *A show where people dress up and act out the Christmas story
test: «The beauty pageant was judged on Saturday.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | A race for runners | A grand, colourful display of flowers | *A beauty contest | A show about the history of a castle
exam: In «The pageant in our town showed the history of the castle», what does pageant mean? | *A show where people dress up and act out scenes from history | A type of hat | A kind of castle | A race for runners
